{
  "summary": "Revision round 3: fixed only the two open R8 findings (plus a compile error left in the working tree). QA-2: added ASwitchedOffPerson_AtTheGoogleCallback_IsRefused_AndNoSessionIsCreated, which drives the real /api/auth/google/complete endpoint with an external (Google) cookie for a switched-off person whose email Google verified, and asserts the callback redirects to /login?error=switched_off and creates no session - so deleting the guard at GoogleSignIn.cs:113 now fails a test. To drive the callback without Google, the in-memory test host gained a Google-enabled mode and a test-only middleware that plants the external identity cookie from a header. QA-1: added BuildStartedByASwitchedOffTeammate_StillShowsTheirName (MariaDB suite), which starts a build as an Operator teammate, switches them off, and proves both GET /api/builds/{id} and the project's build history still show their name (BuildRecord.Initiator is snapshotted at start and stored in the build's Data JSON). Also removed a stray duplicate 'using System.Security.Claims;' and an unqualified System.* reference at the end of BuildRouter.cs that stopped the server compiling. No other behaviour changed. Full backend suite: 904 passed, 0 failed, 76 skipped (MariaDB-gated).",
